    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2VncZsisuSw6LY8LZia9364)_\n\nFollow-up to #271. Every change works with the current yadm setup and with the Stow layout, so it can be merged before you run the cutover.\n\n- `emacs-pr.fish`: uses `git -C ~/dotfiles` when that repo exists (else `yadm`) and finds the config under `emacs-modular/.config/emacs-modular` when the checkout has the Stow layout.\n- `sp-globals`: new `sp-dotfiles-dir` (`~/dotfiles/`) and `sp-dotfiles-work-tree`; `sp-yadm-repo` defaults to `~/dotfiles/.git` when it exists, so `sp-org-issues` worktrees follow it.\n- `sp-vcontrol`: `M-x yadm` opens Magit on the dotfiles work tree; `vc-follow-symlinks` is `t` so Magit finds the repo through the links.\n- `sp-agenda-views`: the config view lists Org files from the same work tree.\n- `sp-env`: comment and doc say `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` is only needed while yadm is used (left in the list).\n- Org docs edited together with the `.el` files; CHANGELOG entry added.\n\nNot run in Emacs or fish (neither is in the container); the `tangle` check is the real test for the `.el`/doc match.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCrRWec3LtT3WLhGCc)_",
    "changed_files": 12,
    "closed_at": "2026-11-03T00:42:50Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "OWNER",
            "body": "The `tangle` check fails on `libraries/modules/text/sp-org-ext.el`, which this PR does not touch. It is already red on `main`: commit d670747 (\"try removing .authinfo cleanly\") removed `(require 'sp-org-node-mem)` and its `;;;;; ID-based workflows` heading from the `.el` only, so `docs/tangles/text/sp-org-ext.org` still tangles them back. The fix is to remove the same 3 lines from that doc. I have not put it in this PR, because it undoes or confirms a change made on `main` and is Sia's call.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
